Privacy Policy
Lumen Drift by BR Dev Team — a CROWNSHARD studio

Last updated: November 20, 2026

Short version
Lumen Drift collects no personal data whatsoever. No tracking, no cookies, nothing stored on our end. What you play stays with you.

Introduction
This Privacy Policy explains how Lumen Drift ("we", "our", or "the game"), developed by BR Dev Team under CROWNSHARD, handles information when you play. We built Lumen Drift to be entirely self-contained — no servers, no accounts, no data leaving your device.

Information We Collect
We collect no personal information — none at all. This includes:

No names, emails, or account details. No device identifiers or IP addresses. No location data. No gameplay statistics or telemetry. No crash reports that identify you. No cookies or tracking pixels of any kind.

Lumen Drift runs entirely on your device and never transmits data to us or any third party.

Third-Party Services
Lumen Drift does not use third-party analytics, ad networks, crash reporters, or social SDKs. There is no data to share because there is no data to begin with.

Cookies and Tracking
We do not use cookies, fingerprinting, local storage for tracking, or any form of cross-session or cross-device tracking. Any local saves on your device — such as game progress or settings — remain on your device and are never sent anywhere.

Children's Privacy
Lumen Drift does not collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13. Because no data is collected at all, the game is safe to play from a data privacy perspective regardless of age.

Changes to This Policy
If this policy changes — for example, if we introduce online features in a future update — we will update the "Last updated" date above and inform players through the appropriate channels. Any new data practices will be described here before they take effect.

